1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:03,878
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

2
00:00:03,962 --> 00:00:08,299
[MAMANG SASTRE PLAYING]

3
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:10,802
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

4
00:00:10,885 --> 00:00:12,721
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

5
00:00:17,058 --> 00:00:17,892
Gavin: You're always
smiling

6
00:00:17,976 --> 00:00:19,811
whenever you’re typing
on your phone.

7
00:00:19,894 --> 00:00:20,687
Oh, who is that?

8
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:21,896
Rommel: Chanty.

9
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:22,480
Gavin: Chanty.

10
00:00:22,564 --> 00:00:23,398
Rommel: Chanty of…

11
00:00:23,481 --> 00:00:24,733
ChantyPop Sweethearts.

12
00:00:24,816 --> 00:00:26,151
Karla: Rommel Romero.

13
00:00:26,234 --> 00:00:27,694
How did you know
my surname?

14
00:00:28,319 --> 00:00:29,320
Don't you remember
me?

15
00:00:29,404 --> 00:00:32,824
I called you because
of this.

16
00:00:32,907 --> 00:00:33,867
- Paldo: Zombie run.
- Velma: Zombie run.

17
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:35,452
[growling]

18
00:00:36,119 --> 00:00:37,829
This is a new side effect.
[music continues]

19
00:00:37,912 --> 00:00:40,498
Laboratory head: Perhaps we should pause
with the trials first.

20
00:00:40,582 --> 00:00:42,417
Perhaps you should
continue

21
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:43,960
with the brainwash, huh.

22
00:00:44,043 --> 00:00:45,003
Atoy: You're not sulking
anymore?

23
00:00:45,086 --> 00:00:47,297
The only reason I was sulking
is because…

24
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:49,758
Audrey: I miss this kind
of bonding.

25
00:00:49,841 --> 00:00:51,050
Atoy: But of course,
I can't

26
00:00:51,134 --> 00:00:53,720
promise that I won't
be busy.

27
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:56,556
But I would always
find time for us.

28
00:00:56,639 --> 00:00:59,893
Atoy: "Deliver 10 boxes of
bacon for F. Cohen.

29
00:00:59,976 --> 00:01:01,561
Pull out, 5 PM."

30
00:01:01,644 --> 00:01:02,771
Who is F. Cohen?

31
00:01:02,854 --> 00:01:04,397
That's Samir's alias.

32
00:01:04,481 --> 00:01:05,815
We need to follow him now.

33
00:01:05,899 --> 00:01:06,566
When, Sir?

34
00:01:06,649 --> 00:01:08,485
At the same time as Audrey's
zombie run.

35
00:01:08,568 --> 00:01:09,360
Jesabel: Why are you dressed up?

36
00:01:09,444 --> 00:01:10,487
You're not coming
with us.

37
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:11,654
I just have a gut feeling

38
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:13,239
that you're gonna be needing
backup.

39
00:01:13,323 --> 00:01:14,949
Jesabel: Oh, suit yourself.

40
00:01:15,033 --> 00:01:16,826
Who is this Belladonna anyway?

41
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:18,870
Rommel: Gavin, maybe we shouldn't
join yet.

42
00:01:18,953 --> 00:01:20,371
Come on, let's just hang out
somewhere else.

43
00:01:20,455 --> 00:01:20,997
Gavin: We can't,

44
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:22,749
I promised to support
Aunt Audrey.

45
00:01:22,832 --> 00:01:23,416
Ah, no, no, no.

46
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:24,375
We'll just be zombies.

47
00:01:24,459 --> 00:01:25,710
Come on, come on, come on.

48
00:01:25,794 --> 00:01:26,628
Huh?

49
00:01:28,087 --> 00:01:29,339
[growling]

50
00:01:29,422 --> 00:01:30,340
[music continues]

51
00:01:33,802 --> 00:01:34,427
Atoy: Where are you now?

52
00:01:34,511 --> 00:01:35,553
Belladonna on the phone: Positive, Sir.

53
00:01:35,637 --> 00:01:36,888
They're loading something
into the van.

54
00:01:36,971 --> 00:01:37,472
Oh okay, okay.

55
00:01:37,555 --> 00:01:38,807
Just keep wa--watch
over that.

56
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:40,183
And then, ah, keep
me posted.

57
00:01:40,266 --> 00:01:43,645
A certain Belladonna
texted Atoy.

58
00:01:43,728 --> 00:01:45,438
So, I'll keep an eye
on my husband.

59
00:01:45,522 --> 00:01:46,940
Audrey: I'm joining
the run!

60
00:01:47,023 --> 00:01:49,109
I'm already in costume
too, love.

61
00:01:49,192 --> 00:01:49,943
Okay.

62
00:01:50,026 --> 00:01:51,152
[music swells]

63
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:54,280
Why?

64
00:01:54,364 --> 00:01:55,865
Why were we assigned
here

65
00:01:55,949 --> 00:01:57,700
on a road where
nothing happens?

66
00:01:57,784 --> 00:01:59,410
What are we? Tree guards?

67
00:02:00,453 --> 00:02:01,830
Chief is so absurd.

68
00:02:01,913 --> 00:02:02,997
You know, Sir,

69
00:02:03,081 --> 00:02:04,958
that's abuse of power!

70
00:02:05,041 --> 00:02:05,667
[hushes]

71
00:02:05,750 --> 00:02:06,918
Shut up.

72
00:02:07,001 --> 00:02:07,836
We've been demoted already.

73
00:02:07,919 --> 00:02:09,379
Someone might hear you.

74
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:12,507
- Someone might hear you.
- Matangbaka!

75
00:02:12,590 --> 00:02:13,550
Yes, Sir?

76
00:02:14,092 --> 00:02:15,009
Change of assignment.

77
00:02:15,927 --> 00:02:17,554
Move closer to Esguerra Oval.

78
00:02:17,637 --> 00:02:18,888
Ah, wh--why?

79
00:02:18,972 --> 00:02:20,807
Ah, was there an
incident there?

80
00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:23,601
None. Additional marshals are needed
at the zombie run.

81
00:02:23,685 --> 00:02:24,811
Help out.

82
00:02:24,894 --> 00:02:26,479
Hurry up, it's starting already.

83
00:02:26,563 --> 00:02:28,439
[sneaky music playing]

84
00:02:31,025 --> 00:02:34,195
Sir, what will we even do
at that zombie run?

85
00:02:34,904 --> 00:02:35,947
That's the thing.

86
00:02:36,030 --> 00:02:37,657
Our time is being wasted.

87
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:41,619
Instead of building a case
against that Atoy!

88
00:02:41,703 --> 00:02:43,246
[music fades]

89
00:02:43,329 --> 00:02:45,874
Sir, what's our plan?

90
00:02:47,417 --> 00:02:48,918
[suspicious music playing]

91
00:02:49,002 --> 00:02:49,961
None. We'll follow orders,

92
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:50,920
we've been demoted.

93
00:02:51,004 --> 00:02:52,005
Come on.

94
00:02:52,088 --> 00:02:53,423
What a great plan, Sir.

95
00:02:53,923 --> 00:02:56,217
[music continues]

96
00:03:01,431 --> 00:03:03,057
[theme music playing]

97
00:03:03,141 --> 00:03:05,143
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

98
00:03:06,269 --> 00:03:09,272
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

99
00:03:11,441 --> 00:03:13,234
♪ Wait a moment, Mr. Tailor ♪

100
00:03:13,318 --> 00:03:15,028
♪ Can you be the one to stitch up ♪

101
00:03:15,111 --> 00:03:16,613
♪ The hole in my polo

102
00:03:16,696 --> 00:03:18,907
that's right under the armpit ♪

103
00:03:18,990 --> 00:03:20,825
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

104
00:03:20,909 --> 00:03:22,869
♪ There’s a secret behind it ♪

105
00:03:22,952 --> 00:03:24,454
♪ If your measurement is wrong,

106
00:03:24,537 --> 00:03:29,542
the whole fit turns crooked… ♪

107
00:03:29,626 --> 00:03:30,293
[gunshots]

108
00:03:30,376 --> 00:03:31,961
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

109
00:03:32,045 --> 00:03:33,880
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

110
00:03:33,963 --> 00:03:35,632
[music swells]

111
00:03:37,759 --> 00:03:39,636
[music fades]

112
00:03:41,554 --> 00:03:43,264
Go, Tabang Lupa peeps!

113
00:03:43,973 --> 00:03:46,309
Oh, Ame, come on! Join us.

114
00:03:46,392 --> 00:03:48,144
Oh, what is that?

115
00:03:48,228 --> 00:03:49,145
Your ride.

116
00:03:50,813 --> 00:03:52,607
Oh, don't refuse it anymore.

117
00:03:53,608 --> 00:03:55,026
I'll push you.

118
00:03:55,109 --> 00:03:56,486
I already registered you,
you know.

119
00:03:56,569 --> 00:03:57,111
Let's go.

120
00:03:57,195 --> 00:03:58,446
Thank you, Paldo!

121
00:03:58,529 --> 00:03:59,322
But why?

122
00:04:00,073 --> 00:04:01,366
Didn't you say you
wanted to join?

123
00:04:01,449 --> 00:04:02,075
Here it is!

124
00:04:03,159 --> 00:04:04,410
Come on, let's go.

125
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:06,371
Oh.

126
00:04:06,454 --> 00:04:07,121
Hold on, okay.

127
00:04:07,205 --> 00:04:07,789
Okay.

128
00:04:08,998 --> 00:04:09,540
Let's go.

129
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:12,877
Here we come, here
we come.

130
00:04:12,961 --> 00:04:14,003
Emerson!

131
00:04:14,087 --> 00:04:15,713
Mmm? Hmm?

132
00:04:16,422 --> 00:04:17,465
Oh, she's in.

133
00:04:17,548 --> 00:04:18,174
Mmm.

134
00:04:18,258 --> 00:04:18,800
This is her, her ribbon, look.

135
00:04:18,883 --> 00:04:20,134
Wait, wait, wait,
wait, wait.

136
00:04:20,218 --> 00:04:21,302
Let me just
remind you

137
00:04:21,386 --> 00:04:22,595
of our mission, okay.

138
00:04:22,679 --> 00:04:24,764
That's the reason we're
here, okay.

139
00:04:24,847 --> 00:04:25,473
Of course.

140
00:04:25,556 --> 00:04:27,517
This, there.

141
00:04:28,518 --> 00:04:29,435
That face.

142
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:31,729
Remember, that's the
two-timing Elvis.

143
00:04:32,605 --> 00:04:34,440
That's who we're looking for, hmm.

144
00:04:35,024 --> 00:04:36,776
Isn't that Elvis?

145
00:04:37,652 --> 00:04:38,278
There, look.

146
00:04:39,904 --> 00:04:40,697
That's him.

147
00:04:41,572 --> 00:04:42,532
It is him, hmm.

148
00:04:44,867 --> 00:04:50,039
We should also find that
slutty Rochelle,

149
00:04:51,749 --> 00:04:54,752
so we can catch them in
the act together.

150
00:04:54,836 --> 00:04:57,255
[sneaky music playing]

151
00:04:57,338 --> 00:04:58,548
My blood really boils

152
00:04:58,631 --> 00:05:00,466
at those home-wreckers.

153
00:05:00,550 --> 00:05:02,552
Damn them, no conscience,

154
00:05:02,635 --> 00:05:03,803
no integrity!

155
00:05:06,014 --> 00:05:07,056
[music swells]

156
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:10,268
As for me, when I’m in love…
I stick to one.

157
00:05:11,644 --> 00:05:13,146
I don't cheat on women.

158
00:05:13,229 --> 00:05:15,940
[playful music playing]

159
00:05:25,074 --> 00:05:26,326
[music fades]

160
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:27,910
Karla: Cool, ah!

161
00:05:27,994 --> 00:05:29,454
It's like nothing has
changed, dude.

162
00:05:29,537 --> 00:05:31,289
Winner, bro, ah!
Nice.

163
00:05:31,372 --> 00:05:32,290
That's so unfair.

164
00:05:32,373 --> 00:05:34,083
The deal was we'd both
wear costumes.

165
00:05:34,584 --> 00:05:35,418
It's a prank!

166
00:05:35,501 --> 00:05:36,210
[chuckles]

167
00:05:36,711 --> 00:05:39,130
Jona: All zombies!

168
00:05:39,213 --> 00:05:42,341
Please go to the zombies'
assembling area now!

169
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:44,177
Oh, there, bro!
You can do it!

170
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:46,179
Just let us slip through
later, okay.

171
00:05:46,763 --> 00:05:48,890
You can do it, bro.
Go on.

172
00:05:48,973 --> 00:05:50,183
I need to hide…

173
00:05:50,266 --> 00:05:51,476
… your face because he
might see you--

174
00:05:51,976 --> 00:05:53,352
- Oop, sorry.
- Miss!

175
00:05:53,436 --> 00:05:54,937
[pensive music playing]

176
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:55,605
Ah, miss, not there!

177
00:05:56,147 --> 00:05:57,523
Oh, baby girl!

178
00:05:57,607 --> 00:05:59,442
We’re about to start,
take your positions.

179
00:05:59,525 --> 00:06:01,694
Runners, are you ready?!

180
00:06:01,778 --> 00:06:04,447
Runners: Let's go!

181
00:06:04,530 --> 00:06:05,698
Yeah!

182
00:06:05,782 --> 00:06:07,658
More! That's it! Like that!

183
00:06:07,742 --> 00:06:08,576
[cheering]

184
00:06:08,659 --> 00:06:11,120
Okay, okay, okay!
But before we start,

185
00:06:11,204 --> 00:06:12,705
a few reminders.

186
00:06:12,789 --> 00:06:14,916
Do not hurt the zombies, okay.

187
00:06:14,999 --> 00:06:15,666
[chuckles]

188
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:17,418
Jona: Right?
Okay, runners!

189
00:06:17,919 --> 00:06:19,670
You each have five ribbons.

190
00:06:19,754 --> 00:06:20,546
Does everyone have them?

191
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:23,007
- Show me! Okay, yes.
- Runners: Yes!

192
00:06:23,091 --> 00:06:24,842
Jona: Perfect!
So, 5 ribbons,

193
00:06:24,926 --> 00:06:26,677
that means 5 lives.

194
00:06:26,761 --> 00:06:27,887
So, take care of them

195
00:06:27,970 --> 00:06:30,014
so you’ll stay alive until
the end of the run.

196
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:31,224
Okay?

197
00:06:31,307 --> 00:06:33,518
Zombies must not
touch you.

198
00:06:33,601 --> 00:06:35,103
The only things they can
grab and pull

199
00:06:35,186 --> 00:06:36,562
are your ribbons.

200
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:39,107
Do we understand
each other?!

201
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:40,191
Runners: Yes!

202
00:06:40,274 --> 00:06:41,067
Karla: Let's go!

203
00:06:41,150 --> 00:06:42,068
Jona: Are you ready?!

204
00:06:42,151 --> 00:06:42,819
Runners: Yeah!

205
00:06:42,902 --> 00:06:44,904
Jona: Okay! On your mark!

206
00:06:44,987 --> 00:06:45,571
Okay.

207
00:06:46,155 --> 00:06:46,948
Let's stay at the back.

208
00:06:47,615 --> 00:06:53,037
Get, set, go!

209
00:06:53,121 --> 00:06:53,913
[whooping]

210
00:06:53,996 --> 00:06:54,497
[action music playing]

211
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:56,165
Jona: Enjoy, enjoy, enjoy!

212
00:06:56,249 --> 00:06:57,750
[ominous music playing]

213
00:06:58,501 --> 00:06:59,377
Laboratory head: This is bad.

214
00:07:03,172 --> 00:07:06,050
[music continues]

215
00:07:07,802 --> 00:07:09,512
He was worthless.

216
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:15,435
He had no information about Belladonna,
Atoy or Mercado.

217
00:07:15,518 --> 00:07:16,978
Trash.

218
00:07:17,937 --> 00:07:23,067
[suspicious music playing]

219
00:07:24,986 --> 00:07:26,362
Sir, update from the bank.

220
00:07:27,029 --> 00:07:28,197
They're ready to leave.

221
00:07:28,281 --> 00:07:29,532
Good.

222
00:07:29,615 --> 00:07:31,200
You go to the meeting
place,

223
00:07:31,742 --> 00:07:33,411
and bring the trash
with you.

224
00:07:33,494 --> 00:07:35,663
Sir, where do we dispose
of the body?

225
00:07:35,746 --> 00:07:37,206
It's up to you.

226
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:38,583
[music continues]

227
00:07:38,666 --> 00:07:39,250
Go.

228
00:07:41,377 --> 00:07:43,588
[rousing music playing]

229
00:07:46,757 --> 00:07:48,050
Hello, Master Cutter.

230
00:07:48,134 --> 00:07:49,010
Be advised.

231
00:07:49,594 --> 00:07:51,679
Target vehicle is
on the move.

232
00:07:51,762 --> 00:07:53,097
We are shadowing target.

233
00:07:53,181 --> 00:07:54,724
Jesabel is behind the wheel.

234
00:07:54,807 --> 00:07:57,185
[tense music playing]

235
00:08:01,230 --> 00:08:02,231
[music fades]

236
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:06,277
[screaming & growling]

237
00:08:06,986 --> 00:08:08,362
You can't take my
life, brother!

238
00:08:08,446 --> 00:08:09,447
[squeals]

239
00:08:09,530 --> 00:08:10,990
Oh my gosh!

240
00:08:11,073 --> 00:08:14,702
[growling & screaming]

241
00:08:14,785 --> 00:08:16,829
You can't take my life,
Zombie bro!

242
00:08:16,913 --> 00:08:18,789
Oh! Safe zone, safe zone!

243
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:21,125
What? Can you still do it?
Aren't you scared?

244
00:08:21,209 --> 00:08:22,960
No. My partner is so
strong, look.

245
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:24,337
Wow, nice.

246
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:25,630
Come on, come on.

247
00:08:25,713 --> 00:08:27,256
Oh no, no, no!
Here they come!

248
00:08:28,174 --> 00:08:28,925
Gavin?!

249
00:08:29,008 --> 00:08:30,092
Gavin?! That's Gavin.

250
00:08:30,176 --> 00:08:34,013
Gavin! Gavin!

251
00:08:34,972 --> 00:08:36,015
[music fades]

252
00:08:36,098 --> 00:08:37,725
[soft rock music playing]

253
00:08:37,808 --> 00:08:38,684
Oh?

254
00:08:38,768 --> 00:08:40,102
There's the zombie
run, look.

255
00:08:40,186 --> 00:08:41,938
It's close to Master Cutter's
event.

256
00:08:42,021 --> 00:08:44,232
[screaming & growling]

257
00:08:45,233 --> 00:08:47,068
Oh, again. Let's focus
on the task.

258
00:08:47,568 --> 00:08:48,903
What are you saying?

259
00:08:48,986 --> 00:08:51,155
When I chat, I'm no
longer focused?

260
00:08:51,697 --> 00:08:52,365
I'm focused.

261
00:08:52,448 --> 00:08:53,908
Sorry, no offense meant.

262
00:08:53,991 --> 00:08:55,576
I'm just reminding you.

263
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:56,577
Okay, many--

264
00:08:56,661 --> 00:08:57,578
Shh. Stop arguing.

265
00:08:57,662 --> 00:09:00,706
That's enough. Jesabel,
focus.

266
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:03,209
Don't stay too close,
we’ll get noticed.

267
00:09:03,292 --> 00:09:04,794
Hey, why? It's just
right, look.

268
00:09:05,378 --> 00:09:07,129
He's right.
Listen to Uno.

269
00:09:07,672 --> 00:09:09,799
[music continues]

270
00:09:10,383 --> 00:09:11,384
Back up a bit.

271
00:09:11,467 --> 00:09:12,426
If we get noticed,

272
00:09:12,510 --> 00:09:13,469
you will get us in
a lot of danger.

273
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:14,887
Why? It's just right,
you know!

274
00:09:14,971 --> 00:09:16,013
Oh, look!

275
00:09:16,556 --> 00:09:18,724
[music continues]

276
00:09:20,851 --> 00:09:21,811
Oh, wait.

277
00:09:23,271 --> 00:09:24,730
Where is this
van going?

278
00:09:26,774 --> 00:09:28,526
That silver car
behind us…

279
00:09:29,652 --> 00:09:30,778
I've noticed,

280
00:09:30,861 --> 00:09:32,530
it's been following
us for a while.

281
00:09:32,613 --> 00:09:34,865
[suspicious music playing]

282
00:09:35,366 --> 00:09:36,450
Are you sure?

283
00:09:38,369 --> 00:09:39,870
[music continues]

284
00:09:41,664 --> 00:09:43,499
When I say turn, turn, okay.

285
00:09:45,126 --> 00:09:46,586
[music swells]

286
00:09:46,669 --> 00:09:48,004
[tires screeching]

287
00:09:49,088 --> 00:09:50,590
Oh no, it turned right!

288
00:09:50,673 --> 00:09:51,799
[tires screeching]

289
00:09:52,425 --> 00:09:54,051
[tense music playing]

290
00:10:10,818 --> 00:10:12,570
[tires screeching]

291
00:10:12,653 --> 00:10:14,030
[music continues]

292
00:10:14,822 --> 00:10:15,990
[car door lock clicks]

293
00:10:17,408 --> 00:10:18,326
[Belladonna gasps]

294
00:10:18,409 --> 00:10:20,870
Oh my God.
Am I going to die?

295
00:10:21,370 --> 00:10:23,247
We're going to die.
We're going to die!

296
00:10:24,248 --> 00:10:25,916
Back up!

297
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,126
[ominous music playing]

298
00:10:27,209 --> 00:10:28,127
Jesabel.

299
00:10:28,210 --> 00:10:29,420
Hold on, okay.

300
00:10:29,503 --> 00:10:31,005
[tires screeching]

301
00:10:34,759 --> 00:10:36,636
Get out of there! Get out!

302
00:10:38,471 --> 00:10:39,847
Just hide,

303
00:10:39,930 --> 00:10:41,182
and no matter what
happens,

304
00:10:41,265 --> 00:10:43,017
don't ever show yourself.

305
00:10:43,851 --> 00:10:46,562
Go on, hide.

306
00:10:46,646 --> 00:10:47,480
Now.

307
00:10:49,940 --> 00:10:51,859
So, Uno, are we really
getting out?

308
00:10:51,942 --> 00:10:53,110
[tense music playing]

309
00:10:53,194 --> 00:10:55,071
Yes, we have no choice.

310
00:10:55,154 --> 00:10:56,364
I don't want to get out.

311
00:10:56,447 --> 00:10:57,490
We need to get out,

312
00:10:57,573 --> 00:11:00,201
rather than have them approach us
and see Belladonna!

313
00:11:00,284 --> 00:11:03,120
- What are we going to do?
- I'm scared. I'm scared.

314
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:07,333
[phone vibrating]

315
00:11:10,878 --> 00:11:12,713
First batch of runners.

316
00:11:12,797 --> 00:11:14,882
Let's shorten their lives!

317
00:11:14,965 --> 00:11:16,342
[growling]

318
00:11:16,425 --> 00:11:17,301
[soft rock music playing]

319
00:11:19,011 --> 00:11:19,970
There, here they come.

320
00:11:21,055 --> 00:11:27,353
[screaming & growling]

321
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:43,452
Atoy?

322
00:11:43,536 --> 00:11:44,662
[screaming & growling]

323
00:11:47,706 --> 00:11:50,167
Wait. Aren't you going to
take my ribbon?

324
00:11:50,835 --> 00:11:52,002
Oh, right.

325
00:11:52,878 --> 00:11:54,922
[phone vibrating]

326
00:11:55,005 --> 00:11:55,548
[phone blips]

327
00:11:56,257 --> 00:11:57,341
Hello?

328
00:11:57,425 --> 00:11:58,050
What?!

329
00:11:58,634 --> 00:11:59,552
I told you, you can't--

330
00:11:59,635 --> 00:12:00,219
don't call.

331
00:12:00,302 --> 00:12:01,053
SOS.

332
00:12:01,137 --> 00:12:03,013
[ominous music playing]

333
00:12:03,097 --> 00:12:04,348
Where did he go?

334
00:12:05,766 --> 00:12:06,684
Love?

335
00:12:07,309 --> 00:12:08,686
Atoy!

336
00:12:08,769 --> 00:12:09,979
[music continues]

337
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:10,896
Belladonna on the phone: We've been
cornered.

338
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:12,398
We're on Delgado Street.

339
00:12:12,481 --> 00:12:13,566
It's close to you.

340
00:12:14,233 --> 00:12:14,859
On my way.

341
00:12:14,942 --> 00:12:15,609
I'm on my way.

342
00:12:17,236 --> 00:12:18,988
[foreboding music playing]

343
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:33,961
Chanty: Gavin, over here!

344
00:12:34,044 --> 00:12:35,004
Over here. Here, here.

345
00:12:35,087 --> 00:12:35,963
Gavin, Gavin, Gavin!

346
00:12:36,046 --> 00:12:36,964
Gavin, here, here!

347
00:12:37,047 --> 00:12:38,257
- Over here! Over here!
- Gavin: Wait, wait, wait.

348
00:12:38,340 --> 00:12:38,966
I'm here.

349
00:12:39,049 --> 00:12:41,343
Gavin, Gavin!

350
00:12:41,427 --> 00:12:42,720
Hey.

351
00:12:42,803 --> 00:12:44,430
That's so unfair.
Wait!

352
00:12:44,513 --> 00:12:46,015
Gavin, here!

353
00:12:46,098 --> 00:12:47,600
That's so unfair.
Oh, safe zone!

354
00:12:47,683 --> 00:12:49,351
- Oh, what? What?
- [growls]

355
00:12:50,060 --> 00:12:51,270
Just let me through,

356
00:12:51,353 --> 00:12:52,855
I'm chasing something
important.

357
00:12:53,772 --> 00:12:55,065
Gavin!

358
00:12:55,149 --> 00:12:56,066
[soft rock music playing]

359
00:12:56,150 --> 00:12:57,359
What the heck!

360
00:12:57,443 --> 00:12:58,986
[music fades]

361
00:13:03,324 --> 00:13:04,158
[growls]
[gasps]

362
00:13:04,241 --> 00:13:04,867
You startled me!

363
00:13:05,367 --> 00:13:06,494
Ow. Wait, wait, wait!

364
00:13:06,577 --> 00:13:09,163
[growling]

365
00:13:09,914 --> 00:13:11,665
[tense music playing]

366
00:13:11,749 --> 00:13:13,250
Siony: Oh, it's Oka!

367
00:13:13,334 --> 00:13:14,627
Oh, Oka, you can
do it!

368
00:13:15,211 --> 00:13:15,711
Wait!

369
00:13:15,794 --> 00:13:17,254
Wait, wait, wait!

370
00:13:17,338 --> 00:13:17,838
Emerson!

371
00:13:17,922 --> 00:13:19,131
[cackles]

372
00:13:19,215 --> 00:13:20,382
What now, Oka?

373
00:13:20,466 --> 00:13:22,218
You're our appetizer now,
we zombies!

374
00:13:22,301 --> 00:13:24,261
[growling]
[heavy music playing]

375
00:13:24,345 --> 00:13:25,596
Aargh! Geez!

376
00:13:26,388 --> 00:13:30,059
[growling]

377
00:13:31,018 --> 00:13:33,062
[music continues]

378
00:13:43,197 --> 00:13:45,032
[music fades]

379
00:13:49,370 --> 00:13:51,914
Damn it. Traffic!

380
00:13:53,415 --> 00:13:55,709
Sir, I know what to do.

381
00:13:56,418 --> 00:13:57,461
Let's not continue.

382
00:13:57,545 --> 00:13:58,671
Let's just leave.

383
00:13:59,296 --> 00:14:00,464
Okay, back up.

384
00:14:00,548 --> 00:14:01,382
How will you back up?

385
00:14:01,465 --> 00:14:03,050
[playful music playing]

386
00:14:03,133 --> 00:14:04,426
The traffic is so bad, right?

387
00:14:05,594 --> 00:14:06,637
And that's what we were
ordered to do.

388
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:07,721
We'll follow that.

389
00:14:09,390 --> 00:14:09,974
[music fades]

390
00:14:10,057 --> 00:14:12,726
What is this? Why is there
traffic here?

391
00:14:13,394 --> 00:14:14,186
[car door closes]

392
00:14:14,270 --> 00:14:15,771
What's wrong with
these people?

393
00:14:19,942 --> 00:14:21,193
Traffic again.

394
00:14:22,236 --> 00:14:23,988
What the heck! Damn.

395
00:14:26,323 --> 00:14:28,284
[horn honking in the distance]

396
00:14:29,159 --> 00:14:30,077
[car door closes]

397
00:14:30,703 --> 00:14:31,704
Why is there traffic?

398
00:14:32,204 --> 00:14:32,955
I don't know.

399
00:14:33,038 --> 00:14:34,164
[music fades]

400
00:14:35,541 --> 00:14:37,376
[ominous music playing]

401
00:14:38,377 --> 00:14:43,924
[rustling]

402
00:14:46,969 --> 00:14:48,846
[zipping & rustling]

403
00:14:57,062 --> 00:15:00,316
[panting]

404
00:15:01,817 --> 00:15:02,651
[car door lock clicks]

405
00:15:03,944 --> 00:15:06,196
[music continues]

406
00:15:18,417 --> 00:15:20,002
[horn honking in the distance]

407
00:15:22,046 --> 00:15:23,923
[tense music playing]

408
00:15:32,890 --> 00:15:34,391
Damn this traffic.

409
00:15:35,309 --> 00:15:37,102
[music swells]

410
00:15:37,186 --> 00:15:37,728
Come on, come on.

411
00:15:37,811 --> 00:15:38,437
Come on.

412
00:15:42,399 --> 00:15:42,900
[car door closes]

413
00:15:43,984 --> 00:15:45,319
You need me, right?

414
00:15:46,278 --> 00:15:46,987
Who are you?

415
00:15:47,905 --> 00:15:49,740
I'm the one Samir is
looking for.

416
00:15:49,823 --> 00:15:51,200
I'm the Belladonna.

417
00:15:51,283 --> 00:15:54,620
[tense music playing]

418
00:15:54,703 --> 00:15:56,580
[rousing music playing]

419
00:15:57,373 --> 00:16:00,876
[grunting & groaning]

420
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:01,919
[thumping & thudding]

421
00:16:02,002 --> 00:16:03,837
[tense music playing]

422
00:16:03,921 --> 00:16:04,755
[thumps]

423
00:16:04,838 --> 00:16:05,756
[music continues]

424
00:16:05,839 --> 00:16:06,715
[thumps]

425
00:16:07,925 --> 00:16:09,218
[music swells]

426
00:16:09,301 --> 00:16:11,720
[gunshots]

427
00:16:15,516 --> 00:16:17,810
[music continues]

428
00:16:18,727 --> 00:16:25,234
[growling]

429
00:16:25,317 --> 00:16:28,278
[anxious music playing]

430
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:44,294
37, 14.

431
00:16:45,004 --> 00:16:48,716
37, 14.

432
00:16:49,216 --> 00:16:52,344
14, 14.

433
00:16:53,303 --> 00:16:58,267
37.
37, 14.

434
00:16:58,350 --> 00:17:01,353
37, 14.

435
00:17:01,437 --> 00:17:06,692
[screaming & growling]

436
00:17:14,491 --> 00:17:16,076
Aargh!

437
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:17,619
[music continues]

438
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:19,163
I know. I'm not a zombie,

439
00:17:19,246 --> 00:17:20,372
I'm a police officer,
you know.

440
00:17:20,456 --> 00:17:21,206
[music continues]

441
00:17:21,290 --> 00:17:22,708
What is this?

442
00:17:22,791 --> 00:17:24,877
Why were we sent here?

443
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:26,670
Nothing is happening.

444
00:17:26,754 --> 00:17:28,714
What are we going
to do here?

445
00:17:28,797 --> 00:17:30,049
[chuckles]

446
00:17:30,132 --> 00:17:32,426
But, Sir, I found out.

447
00:17:33,385 --> 00:17:35,304
This Harvest Aid?

448
00:17:35,387 --> 00:17:38,182
This is Audrey Padua's
office.

449
00:17:38,265 --> 00:17:40,100
Guess who her husband is.

450
00:17:40,184 --> 00:17:41,685
My eyesight is just sharp,

451
00:17:41,769 --> 00:17:43,312
but I'm not a fortune teller.

452
00:17:44,646 --> 00:17:45,647
Padua!

453
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:48,192
[music continues]

454
00:17:48,275 --> 00:17:49,318
Who?!

455
00:17:50,277 --> 00:17:52,988
Atoy Padua, Sir! Maybe
he's around here.

456
00:17:53,572 --> 00:17:55,074
Oh, I know that. Padua,
you know.

457
00:17:55,157 --> 00:17:56,366
That's Atoy Padua.

458
00:17:57,201 --> 00:17:57,910
[smirks]

459
00:17:58,535 --> 00:18:00,162
Well, look at that, it
is fate, right?

460
00:18:01,038 --> 00:18:04,041
That guy really keeps bringing
us together.

461
00:18:04,958 --> 00:18:05,542
[smirks]

462
00:18:06,210 --> 00:18:06,960
I know that.

463
00:18:07,961 --> 00:18:09,254
I know, right?
I'm good.

464
00:18:09,922 --> 00:18:11,215
So, you know, next time,

465
00:18:11,298 --> 00:18:12,424
when there's an event
like that,

466
00:18:13,383 --> 00:18:16,887
you should research who really
produced it

467
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:18,388
so you'll know who it is.

468
00:18:18,472 --> 00:18:19,431
Go on then.

469
00:18:19,515 --> 00:18:21,475
What's the name of Audrey
Padua's office?

470
00:18:21,558 --> 00:18:24,353
[pleasant music playing]

471
00:18:26,063 --> 00:18:27,064
[Elias growls]

472
00:18:27,147 --> 00:18:31,235
[screaming & growling]

473
00:18:31,318 --> 00:18:32,694
Where is Emerson, anyway?

474
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:34,154
I don't know about him.

475
00:18:34,238 --> 00:18:35,948
It seems like he's having pregnancy
cravings on Oka.

476
00:18:36,031 --> 00:18:37,491
He's fixating on him.

477
00:18:37,574 --> 00:18:39,827
You know, let's
just focus.

478
00:18:39,910 --> 00:18:42,663
Have you seen our target?
The…

479
00:18:42,746 --> 00:18:43,872
cheating Elvis?

480
00:18:43,956 --> 00:18:45,499
[screaming nearby]

481
00:18:47,709 --> 00:18:48,585
There, look.

482
00:18:49,378 --> 00:18:51,338
[screaming & growling]
[sneaky music playing]

483
00:18:51,421 --> 00:18:52,339
Paldo: Is that him?

484
00:18:53,215 --> 00:18:55,801
- Oh, it is.
- Ame, it's him!

485
00:18:56,343 --> 00:18:57,803
He has so many women with him, ah.

486
00:18:58,512 --> 00:19:00,013
Paldo: Wait. I need to take
a picture of this.

487
00:19:00,097 --> 00:19:04,560
[screaming nearby]

488
00:19:05,394 --> 00:19:06,353
[music continues]

489
00:19:06,436 --> 00:19:07,938
Ame: But he isn't with

490
00:19:08,021 --> 00:19:10,107
that--that Rochelle
the mistress.

491
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:11,400
[screaming nearby]

492
00:19:11,483 --> 00:19:12,484
Wait.

493
00:19:13,110 --> 00:19:14,611
It looks like he dropped something.

494
00:19:14,695 --> 00:19:15,737
- Wait.
- Huh?

495
00:19:18,031 --> 00:19:22,161
[screaming nearby]

496
00:19:24,204 --> 00:19:24,955
[music fades]

497
00:19:25,038 --> 00:19:30,919
[screaming nearby]

498
00:19:35,549 --> 00:19:37,885
[soft rock music playing]

499
00:19:37,968 --> 00:19:38,844
Ame.

500
00:19:43,390 --> 00:19:44,433
[music fades]

501
00:19:44,516 --> 00:19:45,225
Sir.

502
00:19:46,143 --> 00:19:47,436
Oh? Where's the van?

503
00:19:47,519 --> 00:19:49,771
It's gone; they woke up.
They escaped.

504
00:19:49,855 --> 00:19:51,398
Where’s Uno, Jesabel?

505
00:19:51,481 --> 00:19:53,192
Jesabel escaped earlier.

506
00:19:53,275 --> 00:19:54,318
I don't know where she is.

507
00:19:54,401 --> 00:19:56,653
Uno is here; he's wounded.

508
00:19:56,737 --> 00:19:58,405
[pensive music playing]

509
00:19:58,488 --> 00:19:59,865
I'm sorry, I wasn't able to get
here right away, okay.

510
00:20:00,407 --> 00:20:01,909
My wife is keeping
an eye on me.

511
00:20:02,534 --> 00:20:04,661
So, ah…

512
00:20:05,412 --> 00:20:07,247
Um, leave now.
Go ahead.

513
00:20:07,331 --> 00:20:07,915
Take Uno with you,

514
00:20:07,998 --> 00:20:09,291
go to the auto
repair shop.

515
00:20:09,374 --> 00:20:11,376
- Belladonna: Okay, Sir.
- Okay? Take care.

516
00:20:14,046 --> 00:20:16,423
[phone vibrating]

517
00:20:16,506 --> 00:20:17,424
[car door closes]

518
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:19,843
Hello, love?

519
00:20:20,636 --> 00:20:21,887
Oh? Ah…

520
00:20:22,387 --> 00:20:23,513
I'm--I'm on my way
back there,

521
00:20:23,597 --> 00:20:25,098
let's meet at the
finish line.

522
00:20:25,891 --> 00:20:27,434
Yes. Someone just
fainted here,

523
00:20:27,517 --> 00:20:28,310
I just helped out.

524
00:20:29,269 --> 00:20:30,646
Okay. On my way.

525
00:20:31,313 --> 00:20:32,231
Oh, here!

526
00:20:33,273 --> 00:20:34,858
I'll give you one
of my lives,

527
00:20:34,942 --> 00:20:36,235
so you'll stop
bothering me.

528
00:20:36,318 --> 00:20:38,570
Okay? So, deal?

529
00:20:40,197 --> 00:20:41,281
Mmm. You have
no choice.

530
00:20:57,256 --> 00:20:58,048
You don't need to scare
me anymore.

531
00:20:58,131 --> 00:20:59,424
The marathon is over.

532
00:20:59,508 --> 00:21:00,801
[music continues]

533
00:21:02,511 --> 00:21:04,179
Don't be mad at me anymore.

534
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:06,056
I'm just doing my assignment,
you know.

535
00:21:06,139 --> 00:21:07,432
[music continues]

536
00:21:09,643 --> 00:21:13,772
Broski Zombie, this isn't just
about the marathon.

537
00:21:13,855 --> 00:21:16,066
It's about my love life!

538
00:21:16,942 --> 00:21:18,068
Do you know, the one
I was chasing?

539
00:21:18,151 --> 00:21:19,027
That's someone I chat with,
you know.

540
00:21:19,111 --> 00:21:20,445
[music continues]

541
00:21:20,529 --> 00:21:22,990
I really wanted to meet
her IRL.

542
00:21:23,573 --> 00:21:25,033
That was my chance, she was
finally here.

543
00:21:25,117 --> 00:21:27,869
But what?
You stopped me.

544
00:21:28,453 --> 00:21:30,706
Now I can't catch up to her.
Darn it.

545
00:21:30,789 --> 00:21:31,498
[clicks tongue]

546
00:21:31,581 --> 00:21:32,708
Ow, ow.

547
00:21:34,042 --> 00:21:35,335
Are you okay?

548
00:21:35,419 --> 00:21:37,004
My knee, it hurts.

549
00:21:37,629 --> 00:21:39,715
Let's move you there for now.
Come on.

550
00:21:42,592 --> 00:21:43,427
T-Bak: Beautiful!

551
00:21:43,510 --> 00:21:44,094
[cheering]

552
00:21:44,177 --> 00:21:46,054
Wow!

553
00:21:46,555 --> 00:21:47,180
Beautiful!

554
00:21:47,264 --> 00:21:48,307
Isn't it that when there
are fireworks,

555
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:51,059
someone has won, someone
has reached the finish line?

556
00:21:51,143 --> 00:21:52,060
Oh, right!

557
00:21:52,144 --> 00:21:53,603
Huh? Well…

558
00:21:53,687 --> 00:21:56,064
I haven't even reached
my quota yet!

559
00:21:56,148 --> 00:21:56,815
[chuckles]

560
00:21:56,898 --> 00:21:58,400
Well, can we still
catch up?

561
00:21:58,483 --> 00:21:59,735
And where is Emerson?

562
00:21:59,818 --> 00:22:01,445
We don’t want to miss
the fireworks!

563
00:22:01,528 --> 00:22:02,779
True.

564
00:22:03,405 --> 00:22:04,072
Aww.

565
00:22:04,156 --> 00:22:04,656
Beautiful!

566
00:22:04,740 --> 00:22:05,741
Oh, wow!

567
00:22:05,824 --> 00:22:09,786
Aww! Whoo! Ohh!

568
00:22:10,495 --> 00:22:12,414
Whoever finished first
is so lucky!

569
00:22:12,497 --> 00:22:13,332
Yes.

570
00:22:13,415 --> 00:22:15,250
Wow!
[applauds]

571
00:22:15,334 --> 00:22:16,752
Siony: Congratulations!

572
00:22:16,835 --> 00:22:18,128
[applauds & chuckles]

573
00:22:18,211 --> 00:22:19,379
Siony: Oh, they even
do that.

574
00:22:20,505 --> 00:22:24,426
[groaning, lively chatter]

575
00:22:33,852 --> 00:22:35,103
Bro!

576
00:22:35,854 --> 00:22:37,481
Ah, bro, are you okay?

577
00:22:38,315 --> 00:22:39,733
Hey, help him.

578
00:22:39,816 --> 00:22:43,361
Bro! Psst, hey.

579
00:22:43,445 --> 00:22:43,987
Hey.

580
00:22:44,071 --> 00:22:44,905
What is this?

581
00:22:44,988 --> 00:22:45,906
[screams]

582
00:22:46,448 --> 00:22:49,284
[growling]
Hey. Oh no, oh no!

583
00:22:50,077 --> 00:22:51,161
Ow, bro!

584
00:22:51,661 --> 00:22:52,454
[lively chatter]

585
00:22:52,537 --> 00:22:54,956
[laughing & growling]

586
00:22:55,916 --> 00:22:57,334
They look alike, you know!

587
00:22:57,417 --> 00:22:58,794
Velma: Enough, brother!

588
00:22:58,877 --> 00:23:03,590
[lively chatter]

589
00:23:03,673 --> 00:23:08,428
[laughing & growling]

590
00:23:08,512 --> 00:23:12,015
Oh no! He bit him/her! Hey!

591
00:23:13,266 --> 00:23:14,851
Help him! Help him!

592
00:23:14,935 --> 00:23:17,521
Huh?! Why me?!
You, you, you!

593
00:23:17,604 --> 00:23:24,236
[screaming & panicking]

594
00:23:25,987 --> 00:23:27,030
Help!

595
00:23:27,114 --> 00:23:29,866
He turned my ear into
flower cracklings!

596
00:23:29,950 --> 00:23:34,121
[electronic blipping]

597
00:23:34,204 --> 00:23:37,833
[intense music playing]

598
00:23:37,916 --> 00:23:39,876
There's a zombie!
He'll bite Emerson!

599
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:41,211
He'll bite Emerson!

600
00:23:41,294 --> 00:23:43,880
Hurry! They might catch
up with us!

601
00:23:43,964 --> 00:23:45,132
Wait. Don't tell me

602
00:23:45,215 --> 00:23:46,466
you believe there's
really a zombie?

603
00:23:46,550 --> 00:23:47,175
Where are you going?

604
00:23:47,259 --> 00:23:48,927
Ah, tell the remaining
runners,

605
00:23:49,010 --> 00:23:51,138
and everyone else that they
need to go home.

606
00:23:51,221 --> 00:23:52,180
It's not safe here
anymore.

607
00:23:52,264 --> 00:23:53,473
Audrey: I'll find Atoy.

608
00:23:53,557 --> 00:23:54,724
[theme music playing]

609
00:23:54,808 --> 00:23:56,601
I'll get to know you
at last.

610
00:23:56,685 --> 00:23:58,478
[music continues]

611
00:23:58,562 --> 00:23:59,312
Hey!

612
00:23:59,813 --> 00:24:00,313
[growling]

613
00:24:00,397 --> 00:24:01,857
Ahh! Aargh, let
go of me!

614
00:24:01,940 --> 00:24:02,691
Elias: Aargh!

615
00:24:03,275 --> 00:24:05,026
What did Obsidian
do to you?!

616
00:24:05,110 --> 00:24:06,653
Don't you watch
zombie movies?

617
00:24:06,736 --> 00:24:08,572
You shoot them in the head
so they can't live!

618
00:24:08,655 --> 00:24:10,407
[grunts & groans]
[thuds]

619
00:24:10,490 --> 00:24:12,659
Dickson, don't!
Dickson…

620
00:24:13,285 --> 00:24:14,411
You recognize me.

621
00:24:14,494 --> 00:24:15,287
[growling]

622
00:24:15,370 --> 00:24:16,621
Don't, Dickson!

623
00:24:16,705 --> 00:24:19,666
["Mamang Sastre" playing]
